From 5ef10566f3fe473f86f5c47734e738d1e3ec448b Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: telegdyd <telegdyd93@gmail.com>
Date: Thu, 22 Oct 2026 05:21:16 +0200
Subject: [PATCH] jasmine-j0039: OSM/CPRh read-only probe and per-chip table
 (sweetosm=1)

First step of the Gold clock done properly (jasmine/HANDOFF-CPUCLK.md
phase 1). sweetosm=1 starts a thread that, 8 s later, reads the CPR fuse
rows the downstream SDM660 CPRh driver reads (38, 65..71), computes this
chip's CPRh corners (open-loop, floor, ceiling, target quotient, corner
register words) and the OSM LUT with the APM / MEM-ACC virtual corners,
adapted from the Linux msm-4.4 cprh-kbss-regulator.c, cpr3-util.c,
cpr3-regulator.c and clk-cpu-osm.c (The Linux Foundation, GPL-2.0; the
user's OK of 2026-10-22), and logs it next to the OSM block of both
clusters, the Gold CPRh controller (apc1), APM, LMh, the GCC HMSS clocks,
the Gold L2 SAW4 and APCS common, all-zero lines left out. The OSM
sequencer registers and program memory are TrustZone's on stock, so they
are read through TZ's IO read call (SCM svc 5 cmd 1). Nothing is written.
The first version ran inside the platform expert and read fuse rows
36..72: the read of row 36 never completed and stopped the boot there.

Co-Authored-By: Claude Opus 5.5 <noreply@anthropic.com>
